# Cohort-adjusted measurement of age heaping in repeated single-year
# age distributions (Lexis model with smooth age, year, cohort and
# terminal-digit effects)
#
# What the script does
#   step01  download Eurostat population by single year of age
#   step02  identifiability by observation design; classical Myers index
#           and a first (least-squares) cohort-adjusted index for all units
#   step03  least-squares index on ages 23-72; Figure 1
#   step05  Poisson estimator, rank checks, alternative age ranges, Romania
#           common years (preliminary), stability over time; Figure S1
#   step06  score test, wild cluster bootstrap, test-based intervals, final
#           application, simulation study, noise thresholds; Figure 2
#   step07  robustness of the final estimator, digit effects; Figures 3, 4
#           and S2
#   step08  Romania table with the final procedure, two-way clustered score
#           test and multiple testing, comparison on the same age range,
#           check of Condition 2, data-driven spline flexibility, simulation
#           with dependence and other digit patterns
#   step09  decomposition of the classical-adjusted difference on the same
#           age range; weak identification by spline flexibility
#   (step04 of the development version was superseded and is not needed.)
#
# Outputs used in the article (all written to the output folder)
#   Table 1   step06_table1_simulation.csv
#   Table 2   step06_noise_thresholds.csv
#   Table 3   step06_adjusted_index_final.csv (ten largest values)
#   Table 4   step09_decomposition_summary.csv
#   Table 5   step07_table_robustness.csv; least squares from
#             step05_summary_poisson.csv; QAIC from step08_df_qaic_summary.csv
#   Table S1  step02_identifiability.csv
#   Table S2  step09_weak_identification_by_df.csv (see also
